meta:
  origin:
    producer: OECD
    title: OECD Time Use Database
    description: |-
      The OECD Time Use Database provides information on how women and men spend their time. Data are currently available for 30 OECD countries. Differences in survey features, the number of diary days sampled, and the categorization of activities may all affect the cross-country comparability of results. To improve the comparison of time use across countries, the samples are restricted to populations aged 15-64 and activities are aggregated into five main categories: (1) Unpaid work; (2) Paid work or study; (3) Personal care; (4) Leisure; and (5) Other time use. Bulgaria, Croatia, China, India, and South Africa are also included.

      Estimates are average minutes spent in different activities (both weekdays and weekends), reported for the total population and for men and women separately.

      Time use estimates for Australia, China, and Lithuania are not fully comparable, due to difference in the age of reference: Australia covers people aged 15 and over, China 15 to 74, and Lithuania 20 to 64. Time use estimates for Mexico are not fully comparable, due to methodological differences.

      For Belgium, Greece, Hungary, Lithuania, Luxembourg, and Poland, time use estimates for individuals aged 15-64 are the weighted average of time use estimates for age brackets 15-19, 20-24, 25-44, 45-64. For each age bracket, time use estimates are weighed by the share of population in that bracket, based on Eurostat population database. For Bulgaria, Estonia, Finland, Germany, and Norway, time use estimates for individuals aged 15-64 are the weighted average of time use estimates for five-year age brackets, starting from 15-19, until 60-64. For each age bracket, time use estimates are weighed by the share of population in that bracket, based on data from the country's national statistical institutes' population figures. For Lithuania, time use estimates for individuals aged 20-64 are the weighted average of time use estimates for age brackets 20-24, 25-44, 45-64.

      For Japan, activity 4.4 TV or radio at home also includes reading newspaper or magazines. Activity 5.2 Other also includes all transport time, except commuting to work.

      Survey years differ across countries; each country's estimates refer to one national time-use survey. Methodological documentation on the national time-use surveys used for the estimates is available in Miranda, V. (2011), "Cooking, Caring and Volunteering: Unpaid Work Around the World", OECD Social, Employment and Migration Working Papers, No. 116.
